- [x] M0: parity with the Unity prototype
	- [x] gather → deliver loop, mineral + gas, per-building stockpiles
	- [x] construction by delivery (blueprint grows as resources arrive)
	- [x] buildings train units from their own stock; RMB move (loop bug fixed)
- [x] M1: MVP unit building basics: Infantry / Mech / Port, direct movement, no pathfinding
	- [x] Infantry Training → Light + Heavy Infantry; Mech Factory → Tank; Port → Ship (flying)
	- [x] tech chain, training queues (5, cancel = refund), rally points
	- [x] minimal combat: hp, range, cooldown, attack, attack-move, idle auto-acquire, air/ground
	- [x] separation so units don't stack; static target dummies
	- [x] fixed-tick deterministic sim; pause + 0.25×–4×
- [x] M2: automation
	- [x] programs as data (JSON): conditions / actions / build-order steps + interpreter that issues Commands
	- [x] gambit semantics: first matching rule wins, higher rules interrupt, "max N" caps, fall-through when an action is impossible
	- [x] scopes: per unit type (+ shared Army list), per building type, Base
	- [x] build order (ordered steps with live status) + base layout slots edited on the map + muster point
	- [x] posture (economy / defense / offense): set by rules, build order or top bar; read by conditions
	- [x] haul verb: crates between stockpiles; "needs" = blueprint debt or production reserve, net of loads in flight
	- [x] block editor: rules as sentences of clickable word-chips; live "● N following" counts; selected unit's rule highlighted
	- [x] hands-off mode (default): no direct control; hands-on: player orders win until finished
	- [x] objective: destroy all targets, timed; best time; restart with current program
	- [x] starter program (wins in ~2:00 with no input); JSON copy/paste; program saved in the browser
	- [x] commands while paused: any order or program edit made while paused applies on resume
- [x] Tech tree, phases 1 + 2 (Starcraft names)
	- [x] combat attributes: armor, bonus damage, splash, slow; multi-hit weapons
	- [x] supply (Command Center 15, Supply Depot 8), Refinery gates gas
	- [x] add-ons: Tech Lab (unlocks Marauder, Medic, Siege Tank, Banshee), Reactor (two at once), built by the building from its own stock
	- [x] units: Marine, Marauder, Medic, Hellion, Siege Tank (siege mode), Viking, Medivac, Banshee; stim, heal
	- [x] rulesets: Classic vs Streamlined (supply hard/soft, add-ons attached/in-place, abilities manual/auto)
	- [x] scenarios: target range, Outpost, Swarm (+Banelings), Armor line, Air wing; defenders fight back and hold their post
	- [x] automation: supply / sieged / add-on conditions; siege, pack up, stim, build add-on actions; add-on build-order step; supply-buffer and add-on chips in the Build order view
	- [x] strategy lab: in-game (Test in lab) and scripts; experiments in docs/tech-tree-prototypes.md
	- [x] old saved programs migrate to the new names
- [ ] Tech tree, phases 3 + 4: Engineering Bay / Armory research, Bunker + Missile Turret for the player, Ghost Academy, Fusion Core / Battlecruiser, Thor, Orbital / Planetary
- [ ] M3
	- [ ] CCG budget: cap program size ("mana" = blocks, already counted in the editor header)
	- [ ] scripted enemy that runs the same program format (an opponent that builds and attacks)
	- [ ] cards: rules as cards in a deck; can one card's output feed another's input?
	- [ ] save / share programs by link

Open design questions
- Building collision: units still walk straight through buildings (no pathfinding by design so far).
- Drag-and-drop reordering for rules (currently ↑/↓ buttons).
- Should "needs" reserves (2× priciest unit) be a per-building setting?

